{"id":"171faf2a-29b8-417f-abc6-45ba1e903173","object":"chat.completion","created":1784832078,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    # Validate input\\n    if 'payload' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing payload')\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    nodes = payload.get('nodes')\\n    required_symbols = payload.get('required_symbols')\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not isinstance(required_symbols, list):\\n        raise ValueError('Invalid payload structure')\\n    # Build node dict and children adjacency\\n    node_dict = {}\\n    children_of = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        nid = n.get('id')\\n        parent = n.get('parent')\\n        symbol = n.get('symbol')\\n        depth = n.get('depth')\\n        removable = n.get('removable', False)\\n        if not isinstance(nid, str) or not isinstance(symbol, str):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid node fields')\\n        if depth is None:\\n            raise ValueError('Missing depth')\\n        node_dict[nid] = {'id': nid, 'parent': parent, 'symbol': symbol, 'depth': depth, 'removable': removable}\\n        children_of.setdefault(parent, []).append(nid)\\n    # Find root (parent is None)\\n    root_id = None\\n    for nid, ndata in node_dict.items():\\n        if ndata['parent'] is None:\\n            root_id = nid\\n            break\\n    if root_id is None:\\n        raise ValueError('No root node')\\n    # Precompute subtree nodes and symbols\\n    subtree_nodes = {}\\n    subtree_symbols = {}\\n    def compute_subtree(nid):\\n        if nid in subtree_nodes:\\n            return\\n        nodes_set = {nid}\\n        sym_set = {node_dict[nid]['symbol']}\\n        for child in children_of.get(nid, []):\\n            compute_subtree(child)\\n            nodes_set.update(subtree_nodes[child])\\n            sym_set.update(subtree_symbols[child])\\n        subtree_nodes[nid] = nodes_set\\n        subtree_symbols[nid] = sym_set\\n    for nid in node_dict:\\n        compute_subtree(nid)\\n    # Initial retained set\\n    retained = set(node_dict.keys())\\n    # Map required symbols to set of node ids that have that symbol\\n    symbol_to_nodes = {}\\n    for nid, ndata in node_dict.items():\\n        symbol_to_nodes.setdefault(ndata['symbol'], set()).add(nid)\\n    # Preparation for removal: order nodes by depth descending, then id ascending\\n    node_list = list(node_dict.values())\\n    node_list.sort(key=lambda x: (-x['depth'], x['id']))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for ndata in node_list:\\n        nid = ndata['id']\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        if not ndata['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if ndata['parent'] is None:\\n            continue  # root\\n        if ndata['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        # Check if any child is still retained\\n        children = children_of.get(nid, [])\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children):\\n            continue\\n        # Check if all required symbols would still be present after removal\\n        # Symbols that would be lost are those in the subtree of this node\\n        lost_symbols = subtree_symbols[nid]\\n        feasible = True\\n        for req_sym in required_symbols:\\n            if req_sym in lost_symbols:\\n                # Count nodes with this symbol outside the subtree\\n                all_nodes_with_sym = symbol_to_nodes.get(req_sym, set())\\n                outside = all_nodes_with_sym - subtree_nodes[nid]\\n                # Only consider nodes that are still retained\\n                outside_retained = outside & retained\\n                if not outside_retained:\\n                    feasible = False\\n                    break\\n        if not feasible:\\n            continue\\n        # Remove this node\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    # Sort retained IDs by id (string sort is fine for stable tie break)\\n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\\n    return {'retained_ids': retained_ids, 'removal_order': removal_order}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that performs grammar-guided node reduction. The problem: given a tree of nodes with parent pointers, each node has id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. Required symbols list. Must reduce the tree by removing removable nodes (and possibly their subtrees?) while preserving that all required symbols appear in the remaining tree. Also need to consider grammar-valid deletion: cannot remove a node if it would remove a required symbol or if it has children that are retained? The description: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" And \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" Also \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" Use node ID as tie break at equal depth.\n\nThe output should be: \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So we need to return a dict with keys: \"retained_ids\" (sorted list of IDs of nodes that remain after reduction) and \"removal_order\" (list of IDs in order they were removed). Or maybe just \"retained\" and \"removal_order\"? The description says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So likely two fields.\n\nWe also need to validate required fields: nodes, required_symbols. Ensure structure.\n\nAlgorithm: Build tree from nodes. For each node, store children. We need to decide which nodes to remove. The goal: reduce the tree by removing removable nodes (those with removable=True) subject to constraints:\n- Root cannot be removed.\n- A node with a required symbol cannot be removed.\n- A node that has any retained children cannot be removed (because removing it would remove its children? Actually \"Never remove ... a node with retained children\" suggests if a n